WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.860
After explaining definitions from his book
‘Elements’, Euclid went on to explain

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.840
some AXIOMS that would help in understanding
geometry better.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.750
What are axioms, you may ask?
The general meaning of an axiom is a statement

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:27.390
that is universally true and
needs NO proof. For example, we all know that

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:34.180
most humans have one brain!
We just know its true and must be accepted!

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.880
Similarly, Euclid assumed that some properties
were true and did not have to

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:46.160
be proved. He called these truths as ‘AXIOMS’.
These axioms are not restricted

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.780
to geometry, and can be applicable throughout
mathematics. They will help us

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.640
to prove and understand complex geometry in
the upcoming lessons.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:02.809
In this lesson, we will study some of his
axioms. The first axiom is:

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:08.180
“Things which are equal to the same thing
are equal to one another.”

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.270
What does this mean?

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:16.870
Let’s understand with an example. Suppose
Bob and Rob go to a store and

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:22.560
both of them have five rupees. Bob buys a
pen for five rupees and for the same

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.630
price, Rob buys two candies. This means that
the cost of ONE pen is equal to

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:33.540
the cost of TWO candies!
So if later Rob wants to trade his candies

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:39.650
for Bob’s pen, he would have to give
two candies to Bob. This means the VALUE of

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.259
ONE pen is equal to the VALUE of
TWO candies!

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:49.979
In mathematical sense, if a quantity ‘A’
is equal to ‘B’ and ‘B’ is equal to

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:53.070
‘C’,
then ‘A’ is equal to ‘C’.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:57.049
a=b and b=c then a=c
The second axiom states that: “If equals

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:00.509
are added to equals, then wholes are
equal”.

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:07.619
To understand this axiom in a simpler way,
imagine if for FIVE rupees you get

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:13.549
TWO candies and for SEVEN rupees you get ONE
pen. So if you add them

00:02:13.549 --> 00:02:18.219
together, you will see that for a total of
TWELVE rupees you will get TWO

00:02:18.219 --> 00:02:23.859
candies and ONE pen!
In the mathematical sense, let’s say a quantity

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:29.290
‘A’ is equal to ‘C’ and quantity
‘B’ is equal to ‘D’. Then ‘A’

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.379
plus ‘B’ will be equal to ‘C’ plus
‘D’.

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:37.449
a =c and b=d  a+b = c+d
The third axiom says that: “If equals are

00:02:37.449 --> 00:02:42.840
subtracted from equals, then the
remainders are equal”

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.430
Similar to the second axiom, if a quantity
‘A’ is equal to ‘C’ and quantity ‘B’

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.019
is
equal to ‘D’, then ‘A’ minus ‘B’

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:56.199
will be equal to ‘C’ minus ‘D’
a = c and b = d  a-b = c-d

00:02:56.199 --> 00:03:00.419
We will explain the remaining 4 axioms in
the next part of the video!

